# Normalise line endings so the repo is deterministic across Windows/macOS/Linux
# and CI, regardless of each machine's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, files
# written as LF in an autocrlf=true checkout show as permanently "modified".
#
# text=auto  -> Git decides text vs binary and stores text as LF in the repo.
# eol=lf     -> check text files out as LF in the working tree too (no CRLF
#               round-trip), which is what Node/pnpm/Playwright tooling expects.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Lockfile is managed by pnpm; leave its bytes alone.
pnpm-lock.yaml -text

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
